-- Q4: hospitalized due to a fall while traveling abroad; confirmation of the
-- wellness visit was given 8 months after the effective date.
-- Tests the section 1.3 / 1.2 confirmation deadline (month 7): confirmation
-- at month 8 is late, so the policy has been canceled. The underlying
-- wellness visit itself is set well within its own month-6 deadline, so
-- that the confirmation deadline is the only condition in play; traveling
-- abroad does not itself matter per section 4.1 ("insures You ... anywhere
-- in the world"), so hospitalization-in-a-US-hospital is set TRUE as
-- unrelated to the question.
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                           IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                         IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                      IS 1
    `hospitalization ground`                     IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`                     IS 30
    `causes`                                     IS EMPTY
    `fraud month`                                IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                    IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                       IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`                 IS JUST 8
    `dispute arisen`                             IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                     IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`                IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`             IS FALSE
    `written proof of claim month`               IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                      IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                         IS 12
    `confined in us hospital`                    IS TRUE
    `continuous confinement days`                IS JUST 3
    `claim made setting out basis`               IS TRUE

#EVAL covered q4

-- Q5: hospitalized for punching my own face to show off for my friends; no
-- fraud or misrepresentation was committed.
-- A deliberate, self-inflicted act done to show off is neither a sickness
-- nor an accidental injury (it is not accidental at all), so the ground is
-- Neither. Fraud/misrepresentation are explicitly set absent, per the
-- question, so that Ground -- not fraud -- is the operative reason.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                           IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                         IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                      IS 1
    `hospitalization ground`                     IS Neither
    `age at hospitalization`                     IS 25
    `causes`                                     IS EMPTY
    `fraud month`                                IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                    IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                       IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`                 IS JUST 1
    `dispute arisen`                             IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                     IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`                IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`             IS FALSE
    `written proof of claim month`               IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                      IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                         IS 12
    `confined in us hospital`                    IS TRUE
    `continuous confinement days`                IS JUST 3
    `claim made setting out basis`               IS TRUE

#EVAL covered q5

