-- Q9: hospitalized due to my son biting me in the ankle; proof of the
-- wellness visit provided 6 months after the effective date; I was serving
-- as a police officer at the time of hospitalization.
-- Being a police officer at the time is occupational status, not a cause of
-- this injury: the bite did not arise "out of" police service, so no
-- section 3.1(4) exclusion applies. `causes` is therefore EMPTY, not
-- `Police service`. The wellness-confirmation timing (6, within the
-- month-7 deadline) is a satisfied distractor.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                           IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                         IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                      IS 1
    `hospitalization ground`                     IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`                     IS 35
    `causes`                                     IS EMPTY
    `fraud month`                                IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                    IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                       IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`                 IS JUST 6
    `dispute arisen`                             IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                     IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`                IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`             IS FALSE
    `written proof of claim month`               IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                      IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                         IS 12
    `confined in us hospital`                    IS TRUE
    `continuous confinement days`                IS JUST 3
    `claim made setting out basis`               IS TRUE

#EVAL covered q9
